## ClientLab Future Suites

Not urgent — understand existing suites first before adding complexity.

### Streaming responses
- Synthetic server currently returns instant JSON; real inference uses SSE streaming
- Need a streaming mode that trickles tokens over time
- Changes goroutine lifetime, connection hold time, memory pressure

### Variable / long-tail service times
- Real LLM output lengths vary wildly (10 tokens vs 4096)
- Creates head-of-line blocking and uneven connection drain
- Add a suite with heavy-tailed distribution (e.g., lognormal with high variance)

### Longer-duration soak test
- Current tests are 2-3 seconds; connection pool behavior evolves over minutes
- Idle timeouts, pool rebalancing, file descriptor growth
- Add a multi-minute run to observe steady-state drift

### Bursty arrival patterns
- All current specs use constant rate
- Add spike/ramp patterns to study semaphore and queue behavior under transient overload

### Timeout and partial failure
- Current specs test fast 429 rejections but not slow responses or hangs
- Add scenarios: server-side delays exceeding client timeout, half-read bodies

### Resource scaling observation
- Track goroutine count, memory, file descriptor consumption as a function of concurrency and duration
